The parton coalescence concept was applied by a theory group also to the d+Au collision system [77]. They found that _final state_ hadronization mechanism produces the features seen in \(R_{dA}\), namely, the difference between meson and baryons and the Cronin enhancement (see Figure 5.7). A first objection to this kind of treatment would be that such an enhancement was observed also in Drell-Yan processes [78]

